REPRODUCED 2026-09-13 09:50, node against the shipped module:

  $ cat > /tmp/spendtest.mjs
  import { pickRunnerError, isSpendLimitFailure } from "queue/bin/queue-lib.mjs";
  const stdout = [
    "> Bash node queue/bin/queue.mjs addjson A loop stalled on the spend limit reaches the person",
    "a-loop-stalled-on-the-spend-limit-reaches-the-pe",
    "done",
  ].join("\n");
  const picked = pickRunnerError("", stdout);
  console.log("picked:", picked);
  console.log("classified as spend?", isSpendLimitFailure(picked));

  $ node /tmp/spendtest.mjs
  picked: > Bash node queue/bin/queue.mjs addjson A loop stalled on the spend limit reaches the person
  classified as spend? true

It has already happened once for real. queue/history.jsonl at 2026-09-12T12:04:17.518Z: kind digest, exit 0, outcome spend, and the error kept is one of the digest own Bash lines quoting the title of the spend-limit task. The digest succeeded and the loop recorded an environment failure.

Where it is: SPEND_LIMIT_PATTERN and pickRunnerError at queue/bin/queue-lib.mjs:470 and :500. The comment above pickRunnerError already names this risk and mitigates it by only searching stdout when stderr is empty, which is not enough, because a clean run leaves stderr empty. The damage is done at recordRunnerExit line 553, where a run with no task fails on the signature alone whatever the exit code was, and at line 576, where spend with no task is blamed on the environment, so a successful digest sets health unhealthy and a backoff.

The shape of a fix worth considering, not a prescription: the CLI own refusal arrives as its whole output, or close to it, not as one line among a hundred, and it is not prefixed by a tool call marker. Match on where the line sits and what it looks like, not only on the phrase. Whatever the runner picks, the check belongs in a test so the next phrase that reads like a refusal cannot do this again.

Related: a-loop-stalled-on-the-spend-limit-reaches-the-pe adds a macOS notification for a real stall. That task gets worse if this one is not done first, because the false positive would tell the person to go and raise a limit that is fine. Whichever runs second should check the other landed.
